 [R-CA-41]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-04-30","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CA"},{"bioguideId":"G000568","fullName":"Rep. Griffith, H. Morgan [R-VA-9]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-05-12","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"VA"},{"bioguideId":"B001322","fullName":"Rep. Baumgartner, Michael [R-WA-5]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-06-25","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"WA"},{"bioguideId":"F000482","fullName":"Rep. Fedorchak, Julie [R-ND-At Large]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-07-09","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"ND"},{"bioguideId":"V000134","fullName":"Rep. Van Duyne, Beth [R-TX-24]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-07-15","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"TX"},{"bioguideId":"F000471","fullName":"Rep. Fitzgerald, Scott [R-WI-5]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-07-15","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"WI"},{"bioguideId":"M001210","fullName":"Rep. Murphy, Gregory F. [R-NC-3]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-07-20","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NC"},{"bioguideId":"P000609","fullName":"Rep. Palmer, Gary J. [R-AL-6]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-07-20","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"AL"},{"bioguideId":"Y000067","fullName":"Rep. Yakym, Rudy [R-IN-2]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-07-21","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"IN"},{"bioguideId":"W000795","fullName":"Rep. Wilson, Joe [R-SC-2]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-09-08","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"SC"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T19:09:26+00:00","id":"hr569-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-21","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-01-21","text":"Referred to the House Committee on the Judiciary."},"laws":[],"number":"569","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Immigration","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"B001291","district":36,"fullName":"Rep. Babin, Brian [R-TX-36]","party":"R","state":"TX"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-01-21","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><strong>Birthright Citizenship Act of 2025 </strong></p><p>This bill limits birthright citizenship by redefining what it means to be <em>subject to the jurisdiction</em> of the United States.</p><p>Currently, a person born in the United States and subject to U.S. jurisdiction is entitled to citizenship. Under the bill, a person is subject to U.S. jurisdiction if he or she is born to a parent who is (1) a U.S. citizen or national, (2) a lawful permanent resident residing in the United States, or (3) a non-U.S. national (<em>alien </em>under federal law)&nbsp;with a lawful immigration status who is performing active service in the Armed Forces.</p><p>The bill does not affect the citizenship or nationality status of any person born before the bill's enactment date.</p>","updateDate":"2025-04-22T20:43:26Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Birthright Citizenship Act of 2025","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-09-09T14:52:51Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-09-09T14:52:51Z"}
